WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:12.102
Brooklyn practiced with Dirk in her driveway until dark. Then someone on a bike rode past.

2
00:00:12.103 --> 00:00:16.853
"Hey, Brooklyn, want to ride to the Ice Cream Hut?" Jacey asked.

3
00:00:16.854 --> 00:00:22.940
Suddenly she noticed Dirk under the basketball hoop. "Dirk! Why are you here?"

4
00:00:22.941 --> 00:00:28.120
"I can't right now. We're practicing for tomorrow's game," Brooklyn answered.

5
00:00:28.121 --> 00:00:32.605
Dirk wiped sweat from his forehead without looking at Jacey.

6
00:00:32.606 --> 00:00:39.352
He spun around under the net and jumped up, nailing a slam dunk.

7
00:00:39.353 --> 00:00:44.094
"I can't go either," Dirk said. "I'm going to talk to Marv soon."

8
00:00:44.095 --> 00:00:51.173
Brooklyn ran to grab the ball. "Jacey, watch this cool move." Jacey

9
00:00:51.174 --> 00:00:54.155
watched Dirk for only a few seconds. Then

10
00:00:54.156 --> 00:01:01.582
she rode off on her bike without looking back. "See you guys tomorrow." *

11
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:11.481
* * Brooklyn arrived at the gym extra early on Saturday morning. But someone else had obviously arrived

12
00:01:11.482 --> 00:01:19.220
even earlier. A large sign hung above the spectators' section: Sit here, Brooklyn. You're

13
00:01:19.221 --> 00:01:26.624
no coach! Brooklyn gasped in surprise. Someone had gone to a lot of trouble to

14
00:01:26.625 --> 00:01:34.306
intimidate her. "That stupid sign doesn't bother me at all," she said out loud. "It just makes me more determined

15
00:01:34.307 --> 00:01:42.959
to win!" "What's that, Brooklyn?" She was ripping down the sign when Marv entered

16
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.741
the gym. "Nothing." Brooklyn crumpled up

17
00:01:47.742 --> 00:01:53.033
the paper. "It's something." Marv

18
00:01:53.034 --> 00:01:57.284
walked closer. "Or you wouldn't be hiding it from me. Show it to

19
00:01:57.285 --> 00:02:04.363
me, please." She stepped off the bleachers and reluctantly spread the crumpled sign on the

20
00:02:04.364 --> 00:02:10.178
gym floor. Marv read the words and

21
00:02:10.179 --> 00:02:13.357
began pacing. "Is someone on the team

22
00:02:13.358 --> 00:02:19.435
bullying you?" "I've gotten a few messages," Brooklyn said softly. "I can handle

23
00:02:19.436 --> 00:02:22.772
it, Marv." Marv

24
00:02:22.773 --> 00:02:31.163
stopped pacing. "I believe you can handle it, Brooklyn, but that doesn't make it okay. Bullying violates our team and school

25
00:02:31.164 --> 00:02:35.596
rules." "I thought I knew who was sending me the notes, but I was

26
00:02:35.597 --> 00:02:44.105
wrong." Marv picked up the sign. "Always let people know if you're being bullied. I'll show this to the principal when she

27
00:02:44.106 --> 00:02:51.905
arrives. Right now let's prepare for the game." He started toward the gym office with the

28
00:02:51.906 --> 00:02:59.311
sign. "Please don't say anything to the players yet," Brooklyn said. "The team has to focus on the

29
00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:06.652
game." Marv smiled. "You really are a good coach, Brooklyn. You're always thinking about what's best for the

30
00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:16.972
team." Dirk was the first player to arrive. When Marv came out of the office, Dirk pumped a fist in the air. "Whales

31
00:03:16.973 --> 00:03:21.478
Whoosh!" "Whales Whoosh!" Marv said, and Brooklyn joined

32
00:03:21.479 --> 00:03:28.461
in. Noise quickly filled the gym as more players and spectators

33
00:03:28.462 --> 00:03:34.619
arrived. Brooklyn felt butterflies fluttering in her stomach. The Whales had to win

34
00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:48.097
today! In the first minute of the game, the Terriers' giant guard raced down the court and stole the ball from

35
00:03:48.098 --> 00:03:51.860
Jacey. He immediately

36
00:03:51.861 --> 00:03:55.685
scored. Jacey looked as if she might

37
00:03:55.686 --> 00:03:58.670
cry. "Shake it off, Jacey," Brooklyn called.

38
00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:02.180
Jacey glanced at Dirk, who was sitting on the bench.

39
00:04:02.181 --> 00:04:04.861
"Listen to Brooklyn!" he shouted.

40
00:04:04.862 --> 00:04:14.754
Stuart had the ball now. The referee blew his whistle. "Foul! Traveling!"

41
00:04:14.755 --> 00:04:21.364
Marv nodded at Brooklyn. Stuart was traveling, just as she had pointed out in practice.

42
00:04:21.365 --> 00:04:25.067
Seconds later Stuart had the ball again.

43
00:04:25.068 --> 00:04:34.085
"Dribble!" Brooklyn shouted. This time Stuart kept dribbling as he ran toward the net.

44
00:04:34.086 --> 00:04:42.729
He missed the shot, but Jacey grabbed the ball and sunk a basket.

45
00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:46.207
"Teamwork!" Brooklyn pumped her fist.

46
00:04:46.208 --> 00:04:57.738
Both teams raced up and down the court, scoring point after point.

47
00:04:57.739 --> 00:05:02.885
Brooklyn paced the sideline with Marv, calling to players.

48
00:05:02.886 --> 00:05:05.105
"Aaron, try a low pass!"

49
00:05:05.106 --> 00:05:06.567
"Loop it, Jacey!"

50
00:05:06.568 --> 00:05:08.965
"Way to steal, Stuart!"

51
00:05:08.966 --> 00:05:12.575
Brooklyn was pleased to see the players listening to her.

52
00:05:12.576 --> 00:05:19.046
But when she offered Jacey a cold water bottle, her friend wouldn't take it, or even look at her.

53
00:05:19.047 --> 00:05:22.117
"Great fake before that three-pointer, Jacey."

54
00:05:22.118 --> 00:05:25.362
"You're not our coach," Jacey muttered.

55
00:05:25.363 --> 00:05:35.238
The comment stung. Brooklyn swallowed, trying to keep her mind on the game instead of Jacey.

56
00:05:35.239 --> 00:05:40.433
At halftime the score was tied: 24-24.

57
00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:46.749
Marv and Brooklyn were planning plays when the Terriers coach approached. "I

58
00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:53.344
found this envelope by the Whales' cooler. Belong to anybody on the team?" Brooklyn's

59
00:05:53.345 --> 00:05:56.416
name was on the front of the envelope. She

60
00:05:56.417 --> 00:06:04.839
opened it, her hands shaking, and read the note inside: You'll always be a clumsy loser. So

61
00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:11.991
far Brooklyn hadn't let the notes bother her. But this one made tears spring to her eyes. Marv

62
00:06:11.992 --> 00:06:18.506
gave her his handkerchief. "Don't worry. It's clean," he joked softly. He

63
00:06:18.507 --> 00:06:27.212
led her to the team bench. "Take slow, deep breaths. After the game I'm showing this note to the principal too. The

64
00:06:27.213 --> 00:06:32.981
bully will be punished. But right now, kid, I need your coaching help." Brooklyn

65
00:06:32.982 --> 00:06:35.537
sniffled and nodded. Marv

66
00:06:35.538 --> 00:06:40.052
waved over the players. "Gather round, Whales." Aaron

67
00:06:40.053 --> 00:06:44.707
saw Brooklyn wiping her eyes. "What's wrong?" "It

68
00:06:44.708 --> 00:06:49.513
looks like someone on our team is bullying Brooklyn," Marv said. "Huh?"

69
00:06:49.514 --> 00:06:52.471
a few players said. "Is

70
00:06:52.472 --> 00:07:00.780
this about those messages?" Jacey asked. "Brooklyn, maybe you shouldn't coach us today if you're really upset." Dirk

71
00:07:00.781 --> 00:07:05.277
gave Jacey a look. "Brooklyn is helping our team." "Yeah,"

72
00:07:05.278 --> 00:07:10.950
said Stuart. "She knew when I had an opening to steal in the second quarter." "Her tips

73
00:07:10.951 --> 00:07:14.851
totally helped my dribbling," said Aaron. "Marv has

74
00:07:14.852 --> 00:07:19.610
a lot more experience," Jacey said sharply. Brooklyn's tears

75
00:07:19.611 --> 00:07:21.951
had dried. She suddenly

76
00:07:21.952 --> 00:07:30.280
pictured Jacey on her bike yesterday . . . Jacey's frown when Brooklyn and Dirk didn't stop practicing to go to the Ice Cream Hut. Was Jacey

77
00:07:30.281 --> 00:07:33.083
jealous? "Brooklyn will

78
00:07:33.084 --> 00:07:37.493
stay and help me," Marv said sternly. "But Jacey,

79
00:07:37.494 --> 00:07:40.832
you can leave right now. In fact,

80
00:07:40.833 --> 00:07:46.496
maybe you'd like to go talk to the principal about that sign you made." Jacey's mouth

81
00:07:46.497 --> 00:07:53.090
opened and shut, like a goldfish out of its bowl gasping in the air. Brooklyn had

82
00:07:53.091 --> 00:08:00.835
guessed at the same time as Marv. "Did you write those notes to me?" she blurted out. Jacey didn't

83
00:08:00.836 --> 00:08:07.223
answer. She just ran out of the gym. The buzzer

84
00:08:07.224 --> 00:08:12.060
sounded to start the second half. "Play smart,

85
00:08:12.061 --> 00:08:15.074
Whales!" Marv said. Brooklyn stood,

86
00:08:15.075 --> 00:08:21.907
her legs wobbling. Jacey was her friend. How could she . . .? "Focus!" Brooklyn

87
00:08:21.908 --> 00:08:28.731
told herself fiercely. "That's what coaches do!" * *

88
00:08:28.732 --> 00:08:32.802
* The Whales and Terriers continued battling for

89
00:08:32.803 --> 00:08:43.866
points. With forty seconds left on the clock, Dirk whipped around under the net to slam-dunk a shot and tie up the game.

90
00:08:43.867 --> 00:08:53.931
The next time Aaron had the ball, the frustrated Terriers' giant fouled, bumping hard into Aaron.

91
00:08:53.932 --> 00:08:58.626
Now the Whales had a free throw they could take the lead!

92
00:08:58.627 --> 00:09:07.867
Aaron stepped up for the shot—and missed. Brooklyn groaned.

93
00:09:07.868 --> 00:09:15.157
The clock ticked down to twenty seconds as a Terrier raced downcourt with the ball.

94
00:09:15.158 --> 00:09:17.265
Dirk signaled Stuart.

95
00:09:17.266 --> 00:09:21.517
"Yes!" Brooklyn whispered. "It's time to try it!"

96
00:09:21.518 --> 00:09:32.689
She hoped her practice with Dirk the Jedi would pay off before the final buzzer.

